# Owner-approved purchasing policy — October 22, 2026

- Do not impose demo per-minute, per-day, lifetime, per-deposit, per-submission, or per-customer ticket purchase quotas. The former 10-ticket, 100-ticket/day, 3-deposit/minute, 20-deposit/day and $500 deposit caps are retired site-wide.
- Customers may select any available ticket quantity and deposit an amount they choose. Preserve the existing $1 funding minimum and exact, representable integer cents/quantities; machine representation boundaries are not business allowances.
- Enforce actual prize capacity, eligibility, sufficient ledger-backed funds, authentication, ownership, confirmation, idempotency, and concurrency protections. Never enable real payments as part of removing demo quotas.
- Preserve password/authentication abuse protections and reconciliation of uncertain payments. These are security/integrity checks, not completed-purchase quotas.
- Apply this policy consistently to UI controls/copy, navigation and recovery, server actions, database constraints, and all active writers. Do not restore old caps from historical migrations or generic architecture examples.
- Test quantities above 10 and 100, deposits above $500 and more than 20 repeated deposits, retry safety, insufficient funds, sold-out prizes, and clearing funded balances. Keep ledger history and sample data intact.
